ions in the comments change the scope from the issue body. A gitleaks hit on an added line becomes a blocking high finding that ard injects in code. A security review whose aid failed can only return changes. Host mode without a Dockerfile runs aid on the host. The aid gets no network access. gitleaks is included. The plan should follow these decisions.\n- #245 (role image builds for k8s) is still open. This change should target the local executor and leave k8s role images to #245.\n- The starter files belong under internal/roles/. Copying the aid into this repository's own .ard/reviewers/ config is a protected-path change and needs a human. The dogfooding config has only eng-review today.\n- The pinned tool versions and the vendored semgrep ruleset need checksums or digests. A worker without network access may not be able to fetch them, so the plan should say how to get them.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E7Ngo2XJcuUFmpV6U8RXqj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
